Original commit body from aa6cb2d217b53bc5239fa120bd7c7cbed0422176:

The per-EDGE gate WI-zovuz shipped fires only when NO externally-derived name
reaches a redirect, and INV-fumod's own instance is not that shape:
guacamole's `curl -L "$URL" > "$DEST_PATH/$DEST_JAR"` IS reached, by
DESTINATION via `DEST_PATH="$DESTINATION/drivers/"`. The row the item filed is
sourced at MYSQL_JDBC_VERSION, read at line 87 on the FILE symbol while
DESTINATION is read at line 59 inside download_driver -- two source sites, one
sink, so the false pair can be refused while the other stands.

Two pieces:

1. `_source_names_can_reach_sink`, a PAIR-level proof beside
   `_source_and_sink_are_one_call` because neither edge alone answers it. It
   survives unless both sides are known and provably disjoint; None on either
   side, or an empty source set (every source in every other language), keeps
   the pair.

2. `_FAR_SIDE_FETCH_COMMANDS` (curl, wget): ADR-0049 ruling 1 read on a shell
   command. The call hands back a value whose content the far side chose, so a
   redirect capturing its stdout writes nothing this program held. It is
   ADR-0016's prohibition stated positively -- that ADR forbids attributing a
   launched program's I/O TO the shell; this declines to attribute the child's
   BYTES to it. Deliberately not in bash.yaml, which is scoped to primitives
   the SHELL performs.

TWO DEFECTS FOUND WHILE THE UNIT TESTS WERE GREEN:

  The collapsed edge is where the names live. When collapsed sites disagree,
  ir._absorb_per_call_site_key REMOVES the singular key and moves the values
  to `<key>_values`. guacamole's file symbol reads three JDBC version
  variables at three lines, so `env_var` is absent and `env_var_values` holds
  all three; reading only the singular found nothing and defaulted to keeping.

  One fact, two homes, and the second silently won. Gating only
  propagate_taint_structural left the instance standing, because bash reaches
  findings through the DDG arm (which reports analysis_method "structural"
  with walk_verdict "unavailable" when no DDG exists). Both arms are gated and
  both are pinned by tests.

Measured on 15 cohort repositories, every arm cold (15/15): 19 rows removed,
0 new findings, no claim verdict changed category. Live on the item's own
instance, cold: violated(6) -> violated(3), and the filed row is gone.

The residual guacamole row -- sourced at DESTINATION, a name assigned in the
SOURCING script and so mis-read as an environment variable -- is a different
defect with a different fix and is filed separately.

Refs INV-fumod, WI-zovuz.

